rgest degree. A Ritz pair is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"accepted when its residual is at most "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tolerance"},{"type":"text","text":" · λ₂, so λ₂ is relative to itself however"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the weights spread; the value is then the vector’s Rayleigh quotient, a sum over edges. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"dense solver below 64 vertices. O((n + m) · products) time; 31 n "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Double"},{"type":"text","text":"s (34 n from 5,000"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertices, for the polynomial filter), and on the shift-invert path O(n + m) more for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"solver."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"weight"},{"type":"text","text":" gives the weight of the edge at each position, read once per position; a weight of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"0 is no edge."}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tolerance > 0"},{"type":"text","text":". Every weight is finite and nonnegative, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxIterations"},{"type":"text","text":", when given, is at least 1."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside","name":"Precondition","style":"note"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"","type":"text"},{"code":"NoConvergence","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" when the Lanczos run on L⁺ spends ","type":"text"},{"code":"maxIterations","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" matrix–vector","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"products (1,000 when nil) without converging, with the products spent and the Ritz","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"residual relative to 1\/λ₂. The run on σI − L that may come first hands over to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"shift-invert rather than throwing, after 4,000 + 20√n products or ","type":"text"},{"code":"maxIterations","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"whichever is smaller. Each shift-invert product is a conjugate-gradient solve that throws,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with its own iterations and relative residual, after 20,000 + 2n. Below 64 vertices the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"dense solver answers and ","type":"text"},{"code":"maxIterations","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is unused. Only a tolerance below rounding has","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reached the default limits in the measurements.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside","name":"Throws","style":"note"}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/spectralgraphtheory\/graphprotocols\/graph\/spectralordering(weight:normalized:tolerance:maxiterations:)-4aqxc"]}],"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory","doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"references":{"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/NoConvergence":{"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The error an iterative method throws when it spends its iteration limit without meeting its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"stopping rule: a power iteration (eigenvector and Katz centrality, PageRank, HITS), a Lanczos"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"or conjugate-gradient run, or a QL eigenvalue iteration. Named after Eigen’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ComputationInfo::NoConvergence"},{"type":"text","text":"; NetworkX raises "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PowerIterationFailedConvergence"},{